  "result": "All 39 tests pass, including the 16 new ones in `tests/test_t2.py`.\n\n**What I changed**\n\n- `calc/expr.py`\n  - Tokenizer now recognizes `%` and `,`.\n  - `_term` handles `%` at the same precedence as `*` and `/`, using Python's float modulo so `-7 % 3` gives `2`. A zero right-hand side raises `ExprError`.\n  - Added a `_FUNCTIONS` table mapping `min`, `max`, `sqrt`, and `abs` to their implementation and arity bounds. `sqrt` wraps `math.sqrt` and raises `ExprError` on negative input.\n  - `_primary` checks identifiers against that table first and dispatches to a new `_call` method, which parses a parenthesized comma-separated list of full expressions and enforces arity. Unknown names still fall through to variable lookup, so `nope(1)` raises an unknown-variable `ExprError`, and a truncated call like `min(1,` fails on the missing operand.\n  - Updated the grammar docstring with the `call` rule and `%`.\n- `SPEC.md`: added modulo and function-call bullets to the language section.\n\nNo files under `tests/` were touched. Nothing is committed yet.",
